# Emacs :: keys for the marlinos Emacs (built-ins only: fido, eglot, which-key). C = Ctrl, M = Alt

## Survive
C-g :: cancel whatever is happening (press it twice if needed)
C-x C-c :: quit
C-x C-f :: open a file (fido: type to narrow, Enter)
C-x C-s / C-x s :: save / save all
C-/ / C-? :: undo / redo
M-x <command> :: run any command by name
C-h k <key> :: what a key does; C-h f function, C-h v variable
> type a prefix like C-x and wait: which-key lists what can follow

## Moving
C-f / C-b :: forward / back a character (M-f M-b: a word)
C-n / C-p :: next / previous line
C-a / C-e :: line start / end
M-< / M-> :: top / bottom of the buffer
C-v / M-v :: page down / up
M-g g :: go to line
C-l :: center the cursor line (again: top, bottom)
C-s / C-r :: search forward / back (again: next match, Enter to stop)

## Editing
C-SPC :: start a selection (mark); move to extend it
C-w / M-w :: cut / copy the selection
C-y / M-y :: paste / then cycle older kills
C-k :: cut to the end of the line
C-d / M-d :: delete a character / a word
M-% :: replace, asking at each match (y n !)
C-x h :: select everything
M-; :: comment / uncomment
M-q :: refill the paragraph
C-x C-x :: swap cursor and mark (reselect)

## Buffers and windows
C-x b :: switch buffer
C-x C-b :: list buffers (ibuffer)
C-x k :: kill a buffer
C-x 2 / C-x 3 :: split below / right
C-x o :: other window
C-x 0 / C-x 1 :: close this window / close the others

## Projects (marlinos keys)
C-c p :: find a file in the project
C-c g :: grep the project
C-c f :: recent files
C-x p p :: switch project; C-x p b project buffers

## Code (eglot, flymake)
M-. / M-, :: go to definition / back
M-? :: references
C-h . :: documentation at point
M-x eglot-rename :: rename the symbol
M-x eglot-code-actions :: code actions
M-x eglot-format :: format the buffer
M-g n / M-g p :: next / previous error (flymake)
TAB :: indent, or complete when already indented

## Files and git
C-x d :: dired, a file browser (Enter, ^ up, d mark delete, x do it)
C-x v = :: diff the file (vc)
C-x v v :: commit the file
C-x v l :: file history

## Handy
C-x C-e :: evaluate the Lisp before the cursor
C-u <n> <command> :: repeat n times (C-u 8 C-n)
F3 / F4 :: record a macro / stop, then F4 to play it
M-x shell / M-x eshell :: a shell inside Emacs
